      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the inner shaded region within the large square that is not part of the circles. \n\n1. **Determine the Side Length of the Inner Square:**\n    - Since the circles are tangent to each other and to the sides of the square, we can infer that the side length of the inner square (which is the region not covered by the circles) can be calculated based on the side length of the original square and the radius of the circles.\n    - The distance from the center of one circle to the side of the square is equal to the radius of the circle, which is 1 inch. Since the side length of the original square is 20 inches, the side length of the inner square (which has sides perpendicular to the radii of the circles) will be reduced by 2 radii (1 on each side).\n    - Therefore, the side length of the inner square will be \\(20 - 2 \\times 1 = 18\\) inches.\n\n2. **Calculate the Area of the Inner Square:**\n    - The area of the inner square is given by the square of its side length:\n    \\[\n    \\text{Area of inner square} = 18 \\times 18 \\text{ square inches}\n    \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the Area of the Four Circles:**\n    - Each circle has a radius of 1 inch, so the area of one circle is:\n    \\[\n    \\text{Area of one circle} = \\pi \\times 1^2 = \\pi \\text{ square inches}\n    \\]\n    - Since there are four circles, the total area of the circles is:\n    \\[\n    \\text{Total area of four circles} = 4 \\times \\pi = 4\\pi \\text{ square inches}\n    \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the Shaded Area:**\n    - The shaded area is the area of the inner square minus the total area of the four circles:\n    \\[\n    \\text{Shaded area} = \\text{Area of inner square} - \\text{Total area of four circles}\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    \\text{Shaded area} = 18 \\times 18 - 4\\pi = 324 - 4\\pi \\text{ square inches}\n    \\]\n\nPutting these steps together in the Python code to ensure accuracy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the side length of the original square\noriginal_side_length = 20\n\n# Define the radius of each circle\nradius = 1\n\n# Calculate the side length of the inner square by subtracting 2 radii from the original side length\ninner_side_length = original_side_length - 2 * radius\n\n# Calculate the area of the inner square\ninner_square_area = inner_side_length ** 2\n\n# Calculate the total area of the four circles\ntotal_circle_area = 4 * sp.pi * radius ** 2\n\n# Calculate the shaded area\nshaded_area = inner_square_area - total_circle_area\n\n# Print the shaded area\nprint(shaded_area)\n```\n```output\n324 - 4*pi\n```\nThe shaded area within the logo, after accounting for the inner square and the four circles, is calculated as \\(324 - 4\\pi\\) square inches. \n\nTo express the answer as a final boxed form:\n\\[\n\\boxed{324 - 4\\pi}\n\\]",
